.TH FACEAUTH-DAEMON 8 "2026-11" "faceauth 0.10.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
faceauth-daemon \- face authentication service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/libexec/faceauth-daemon
.RB [ \-\-session\-bus " " \-\-state\-dir
.IR dir ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B faceauth-daemon
owns the camera and the enrolled face data and provides the
.B io.github.gvarsanyi.FaceAuth1
service on the system bus. It is started on demand by D-Bus activation
through
.BR faceauth-daemon.service ,
runs as the unprivileged
.B faceauthd
user, and is the only process that opens cameras for face authentication.
.PP
Authorization: root may call every method. Other callers may read and test
only their own account; testing additionally requires that the caller be in
a local, foreground seat session (checked with systemd-logind). Enrolling,
deleting, and changing service settings require the polkit actions
.B io.github.gvarsanyi.faceauth.manage-own
or
.BR io.github.gvarsanyi.faceauth.manage-other .
.PP
Virtual cameras (v4l2loopback, akvcam, vivid) are never used because other
processes can inject frames into them.
.PP
The face models are loaded on first use and unloaded after five idle
minutes. Callers that retry immediately after a failure (the KDE lock
screen does) are slowed down: after two such retries for the same user and
service, each further retry first waits 5, 10, then at most 20 seconds with
the camera off. A success, or a pause of three seconds before the next attempt,
resets this.
.PP
While the user's graphical session is locked (logind
.BR LockedHint ,
set by KDE Plasma and GNOME), a match counts only after the camera has seen
no face for two seconds since the lock, so locking the screen while seated
does not unlock it again immediately. Session agents
.RB ( faceauth-agent ,
one per graphical session) register with the daemon and receive a unicast
signal whenever their user's face is checked, to show a notification.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-session\-bus
Serve on the session bus as the current user, without polkit. For
development and testing only.
.TP
.BI \-\-state\-dir " dir"
State directory; only with
.BR \-\-session\-bus .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/faceauth/<uid>.enc.json
Enrolled camera and face encodings (mode 0600).
.TP
.I /var/lib/faceauth/<uid>.optout
Services the user disabled.
.TP
.I /etc/faceauth/faceauth.conf
Configuration; read on every request.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR faceauth (1),
.BR faceauth.conf (5),
.BR pam_faceauth (8)
